00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:27,120
 and I'm thinking, wow, now there's a mystery.

575
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:28,800
 In order for that to happen,

576
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:31,200
 we need well-defined payment rails

577
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:33,480
 and well-defined guard rails for these agents

578
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,520
 to interact with each other

579
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:38,080
 and sort of end commerce sites or end applications.

580
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:39,400
 And that again is something

581
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:41,760
 that blockchains are ideally positioned for

582
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:44,200
 because they're about enabling you

583
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:46,880
 to make immutable commitments

584
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:48,160
 and make those commitments

585
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:50,240
 part of the running of a software process.

586
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:52,120
 You can basically tell an agent,

587
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:54,120
 you have access just to this wallet,

588
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:56,480
 you have access to just these memory areas

589
00:23:56,480 --> 00:23:58,280
 and you have these search instructions

590
00:23:58,280 --> 00:24:00,040
 that you can't go outside of

591
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:02,600
 other than that, go find anything you can.

