00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:18,600
 We just spoke to Scott about some of his ideas,

600
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:20,800
 including his last ones he was talking about,

601
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:24,120
 sending an agent out to go do his shopping for him,

602
00:24:24,120 --> 00:24:26,040
 which seems like a pretty natural segue

603
00:24:26,040 --> 00:24:28,560
 into what you're writing about,

604
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:32,400
 which is about how crypto in conjunction with AI agents

605
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:35,000
 could potentially help solve this monetization issue

606
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:36,880
 that the web is facing right now.

607
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:39,560
 So let's hear from you, describe your idea.

608
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:42,360
 - Yeah, so this came about through a number of conversations

609
00:24:42,360 --> 00:24:45,480
 that we have internally around what is the next generation

610
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:48,080
 of the contract of the internet look like,

611
00:24:48,080 --> 00:24:51,160
 the original internet monetizing this idea of attention,

612
00:24:51,160 --> 00:24:52,000
 mostly, right?

613
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,640
 So if you think about how Google came about and SEO

614
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,320
 is all direct traffic to your website in return,

615
00:24:57,320 --> 00:25:00,000
 you let me surface your content on Google,

616
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,840
 and this is kind of this fair exchange of sites

617
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:04,240
 get more traffic and Google gets to make a lot of money

618
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,600
 on advertising.

619
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:08,320
 And so what does the next generation of that look like?

620
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:10,120
 - And the reason that we need a next generation

621
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:12,480
 is 'cause that model has basically collapsed now

622
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:14,960
 with nobody needs to go visit websites anymore.

623
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:17,280
 You can just get all the information you need

624
00:25:17,280 --> 00:25:19,800
 from an AI service or even Google

625
00:25:19,800 --> 00:25:21,640
 just putting the information up there

626
00:25:21,640 --> 00:25:23,840
 at the top of the webpage, their AI overviews,

627
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:24,760
 I think they're called.

628
00:25:24,760 --> 00:25:25,680
 - Yes, exactly.

629
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:28,160
 So you no longer need to actually go visit

630
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:29,000
 the underlying site.

631
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:32,480
 You can get these awesome summaries either through ChatchBT

632
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:34,960
 or through Google's One Box or Proplexity

633
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:38,000
 or whatever kind of tool you're using these days.

634
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,400
 Because of that, you're kind of breaking

635
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:41,880
 this economic contract of what is the purpose

636
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:44,560
 of putting that information out into the world for free

637
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:46,560
 as the underlying content site.

638
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:47,840
 If you're not getting anything in return.

639
00:25:47,840 --> 00:25:49,680
 So how do you fix that?

640
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:52,360
 And so I think there's a couple of different ways

641
00:25:52,360 --> 00:25:54,240
 you can approach this and different strategies

642
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:57,080
 people are taking for how do you fix this monetization

643
00:25:57,080 --> 00:25:59,880
 and economic model if we're no longer directing people

644
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:02,680
 to sites and how do you actually continue to incentivize

645
00:26:02,680 --> 00:26:05,760
 new content and the long tail of content on the internet

646
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:08,280
 if we're breaking this economic model.

647
00:26:08,280 --> 00:26:11,840
 It might mean agents go out and just pay per data point

648
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:13,480
 and they go out and as they need more context,

649
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:14,600
 they pay for it.

650
00:26:14,600 --> 00:26:17,320
 The idea I walk through is this more fanciful idea

651
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:19,200
 of what would it look like to do revenue sharing

652
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:20,120
 through transactions.

653
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:22,080
 In my view, people have gotten pretty accustomed

654
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:24,720
 to the web being free and it seems unlikely

655
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:26,720
 that they're willing to kind of fund these agents

656
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:28,800
 to go do search for them when it would be free

657
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:30,880
 for them to go to Google or it's free today

658
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,920
 for them to use Google One Box or Proplexity

659
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:34,960
 or these free versions of the agents.

660
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:38,280
 And so if people aren't willing to spend money upfront

661
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:39,920
 for the agent to pay for the data,

662
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:41,560
 what else might this look like?

663
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:43,840
 And so one idea that I just kind of walked through

664
00:26:43,840 --> 00:26:45,520
 is this idea of transaction sharing

665
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:48,560
 between all the content sites and the end action.

666
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:51,200
 So you send your agent out to shop for you.

667
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:52,520
 If it actually ends up buying something,

668
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:54,520
 there's some sort of revenue share back

669
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:57,120
 to all the places that it got context for that.

670
00:26:57,120 --> 00:26:59,000
 - And by the way, it's cliche to say

671
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:02,720
 that it's actually not free, you're paying with your data.

672
00:27:02,720 --> 00:27:06,520
 But despite that being cliche, it is extremely true.

673
00:27:06,520 --> 00:27:09,440
 The web which seems free is monetized.

674
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:12,880
 It's just monetized in a way that you're not really seeing.

675
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:14,720
 And so even if you're like,

676
00:27:14,720 --> 00:27:17,560
 oh, well, how are we going to add in all these transactions,

677
00:27:17,560 --> 00:27:18,840
 these payments and whatever,

678
00:27:18,840 --> 00:27:21,840
 the thing is all these ad networks have all of that

679
00:27:21,840 --> 00:27:23,960
 there already, it's just not in front of your face.

680
00:27:23,960 --> 00:27:28,040
 So it's not that radical a shift as one might imagine.

681
00:27:28,040 --> 00:27:28,880
 - Yeah, exactly.

682
00:27:28,880 --> 00:27:31,400
 Today you're basically doing this exact same flow

683
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:32,480
 just with extra steps.

684
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:36,480
 So you get served an ad when you go visit a content site,

685
00:27:36,480 --> 00:27:38,560
 the idea being that at some point you will convert

686
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:40,720
 on that ad and actually go buy something.

687
00:27:40,720 --> 00:27:42,600
 And so the company is the ad agency,

688
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:45,800
 the people advertising are willing to pay upfront

689
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:48,320
 for that ad, assuming you will then convert

690
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:49,640
 into a transaction.

691
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:52,480
 The idea is to make that process more direct

692
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:54,560
 given that we no longer have this attention

693
00:27:54,560 --> 00:27:55,520
 on the underlying site.

694
00:27:55,520 --> 00:27:58,400
 So instead of going to Google, getting routed to a site,

695
00:27:58,400 --> 00:28:01,200
 getting served an ad, possibly converting on that ad

696
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:03,640
 and going and buying something later down the line,

697
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:06,600
 that happens all kind of in at one flow through

698
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:09,040
 of when that transaction occurs,

699
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:11,040
 everyone involved in that transaction gets paid back

700
00:28:11,040 --> 00:28:12,120
 automatically.

701
00:28:12,120 --> 00:28:14,080
 And the great thing about that is that the attribution

702
00:28:14,080 --> 00:28:16,600
 is actually possible to trace because the agent

703
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:18,680
 is pulling in context in real time.

704
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:21,520
 And so it's not as kind of intangible as a human

705
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:24,520
 who might visit a million sites and see a billboard

706
00:28:24,520 --> 00:28:26,480
 and see a friend talking about something

707
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:29,560
 and trying to attribute back why they actually bought something

708
00:28:29,560 --> 00:28:32,240
 is a much more complex process than just attributing back

709
00:28:32,240 --> 00:28:33,880
 what the agent used in its path

710
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:36,320
 to recommend to that end transaction.

711
00:28:36,320 --> 00:28:37,720
 - So what are the technical pieces

712
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:41,400
 that need to be in place for this to happen?

713
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:43,280
 - Yeah, so you need the ability to do

714
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:46,800
 these very complex splits of nano payments,

715
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:50,400
 which today is very challenging to impossible

716
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,760
 given just the basic overhead

717
00:28:51,760 --> 00:28:53,960
 of a single credit card transaction

718
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:57,320
 makes it infeasible to do these like a 10th of a cent

719
00:28:57,320 --> 00:28:59,680
 or 100th of a cent or 1000th of a cent transactions.

720
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:01,440
 - And that's because there's just like a basic fee

721
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:02,640
 on a credit card transaction.

722
00:29:02,640 --> 00:29:05,240
 I forget how much it is like 30 cents or something,

723
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:08,120
 like which immediately gets rid of any opportunity

724
00:29:08,120 --> 00:29:10,480
 of doing anything beneath that cost point.

725
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:11,320
 - Exactly.

726
00:29:11,320 --> 00:29:13,080
 And then you would also need to be able to do

727
00:29:13,080 --> 00:29:15,640
 this attribution of what data and context

728
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:17,440
 is an agent pulling in.

729
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:20,080
 And then you would just need a way to actually pay that out.

730
00:29:20,080 --> 00:29:23,200
 On crypto rails, this is as simple as putting in the metadata

731
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:26,520
 wallet address that is paid out to every time you use the data,

732
00:29:26,520 --> 00:29:29,760
 you could even guard it or pay well in that way

733
00:29:29,760 --> 00:29:31,440
 just for agents to scrape it.

734
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:33,360
 But in the traditional financial world,

735
00:29:33,360 --> 00:29:35,040
 this would be significantly harder to figure out

736
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:38,080
 how to actually pay each content provider,

737
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:40,880
 figure out a bank account or credit card number or

738
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:42,680
 how you actually get that money back to them.

739
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:46,160
 So yeah, needed ability to attribute where the data came from

740
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:48,520
 to do these small and complex payment splits

741
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:51,600
 and then actually be able to pay the underlying content creators.

742
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:54,360
 - Do you think that we are going to get there in time

743
00:29:54,360 --> 00:29:58,400
 before AI eats all the good information

744
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:01,680
 and sort of forces content creators to question

745
00:30:01,680 --> 00:30:04,960
 whether they wanna start publishing openly on the web?

746
00:30:04,960 --> 00:30:06,320
 - Yeah, I mean, I hope so.

747
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:07,680
 I think it's definitely feasible.

748
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:10,320
 It seems like today the direction we're mostly going in

749
00:30:10,320 --> 00:30:13,320
 is remaining with the agent as the intermediary.

750
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:16,440
 So rather than you having this flow back effect

751
00:30:16,440 --> 00:30:19,320
 or this revenue sharing effect instead,

752
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:23,200
 the agent companies like OpenAI or Anthropic or whoever

753
00:30:23,200 --> 00:30:25,280
 are paying directly for access to this data

754
00:30:25,280 --> 00:30:27,760
 through these big data deals with Reddit

755
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:29,920
 or the New York Times or whoever.

756
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:32,920
 So then you're paying your monthly subscription to OpenAI,

757
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:35,920
 they're paying an annual subscription to the data provider

758
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:38,760
 and then that data is surfaced in that agent

759
00:30:38,760 --> 00:30:41,160
 that does start to address this issue,

760
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:44,520
 but going down that path ends up with this kind of

761
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:47,360
 very siloed information where you're only gonna get

762
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:49,880
 surfaced information on OpenAI with companies

763
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,440
 and OpenAI has signed deals with

764
00:30:51,440 --> 00:30:53,400
 and you lose the openness of the web

765
00:30:53,400 --> 00:30:55,360
 and especially you lose the long tail

766
00:30:55,360 --> 00:30:58,760
 of individual content creators that can't get these

767
00:30:58,760 --> 00:31:01,240
 partnerships with OpenAI and so their information

768
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:04,680
 is not surfaced the way that it might be today in Google

769
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:06,560
 where even if it's not promoted

770
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:07,520
 so it might not be on the first page,

771
00:31:07,520 --> 00:31:09,760
 you can still always find any data you want

772
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:11,680
 and it kind of gives you this open access

773
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:13,280
 that these information silos might not.

774
00:31:13,280 --> 00:31:15,840
 So it feels like we're heading more and more

775
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:17,960
 in that direction, but hopefully we can make it

776
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:20,320
 a little bit more fair and open.

777
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:23,280
 - Excellent, while speaking of fair and open,

778
00:31:23,280 --> 00:31:25,280
 our website where you can read Liz

779
00:31:25,280 --> 00:31:27,680
 and the rest of these contributions is open,

780
00:31:27,680 --> 00:31:30,720
 not pay walled, so you can go read these posts there.

781
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:31,920
 Liz, thanks so much for coming on

782
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:33,000
 and sharing your idea.

783
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,600
 - Awesome, thank you.

