00:36:26,680 --> 00:36:28,480
 And this was something that Chris and I wrote about

897
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:31,000
 in our blog post about Story Protocol.

898
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:33,040
 About a year ago, we hypothesized

899
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:34,560
 that the social contract of the internet

900
00:36:34,560 --> 00:36:35,680
 was going to fall apart,

901
00:36:35,680 --> 00:36:38,600
 where creators are incentivized to provide their content

902
00:36:38,600 --> 00:36:40,840
 for free so that platforms can index

903
00:36:40,840 --> 00:36:44,120
 and then provide distribution back to them as a service.

904
00:36:44,120 --> 00:36:46,400
 That was like the original social contract of the internet.

905
00:36:46,400 --> 00:36:49,240
 Today, if the primary distribution engine

